WEBVTT

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.400
Strike!

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:09.100
<i>If she stands that far forward, bunting 
for a base hit is out of the question.</i>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.650
<i>I have no choice but to swing.</i>

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.040
Strike two!

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.130
Hey! Snap out of it Daigo!

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:30.880
Quit swinging like you're hot stuff!

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.380
You can't do things you haven't 
practiced, John Doe #28!

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.150
<i>S-Sis?</i>

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.980
<i>Yeah. She's right!</i>

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.660
<i>When your back's against the wall,</i>

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.580
<i>stick to what you're most comfortable with!</i>

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:49.660
<i>What?!</i>

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:57.530
Michiru!

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.020
Safe!

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.380
Nice one, Daigo!

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:43.300
Ace on the Mound

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.910
Daigo's playing well!

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:43.800
You can only pull off a two-strike bunt 
if you're brimming with confidence.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:47.240
That's literally all he 
practiced with Urabe-kun.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.770
Guess he needs to thank me 
for the advice I gave him.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.310
You're so...

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.610
Urabe Hayato

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.610
Pitcher

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.610
<i>Batting third, pitcher, Urabe-kun.</i>

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.030
Touto Boys

00:02:54.980 --> 00:03:00.030
Catcher  Mayumura Wataru

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.610
<i>Didn't think he had the guts 
to try a two-strike bunt.</i>

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.010
<i>Rats! They got us!</i>

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.730
<i>One out, runners on first and third.</i>

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:06.540
Touto Boys

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:06.540
First base  
Mayumura Michiru

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.520
<i>We might be two runs ahead, 
but you've gotta stay sharp, Wataru!</i>

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.290
Mifune Dolphins

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.290
Manager  Tashiro

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.210
It's a squeeze play!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.110
Safe!

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.090
Safe!

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.050
Yeah!

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.200
Nice one, Urabe!

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.230
Mifune

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.230
Touto

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:35.310
Touto Boys

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:35.310
Pitcher  Komatsu

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.250
What are you playing at, Wataru?!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.060
I can't believe we've let them pull off 
two squeeze plays in one game!

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.330
You usually spot squeezes from a mile away!

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.800
Shigeno-kun punished us 
with that two-strike bunt,

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.620
but we're wobbling right now!

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:52.310
Snap out of it, Mister Shot Caller!

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:54.000
We're only up one run 
and their cleanup's next!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.340
Do you <i>want</i> to lose?!

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.860
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.510
Catcher

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.510
Suzuki Andy

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.830
<i>I can't believe I let my nerves 
get the better of me.</i>

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:09.220
Ball!

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.620
<i>They're starting to drift high.</i>

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.880
<i>Komatsu's reached his limit.</i>

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.970
<i>I should've told the bullpen to warm up.</i>

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:21.450
<i>No, this team's cleanup and fifth 
hitter would overpower them.</i>

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.510
<i>Komatsu will just have to 
tough it out for now.</i>

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.840
All right! It got through!

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.040
Run!

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.500
Safe!

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.710
We did it!

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.180
Right field

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.180
Mifune Dolphins

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.180
Sakura Mutsuko

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:45.180
Coach  Fujii

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.180
We tied the game!

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:46.450
Awesome!

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:49.390
Time out, please.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.850
Mifune

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.850
Touto

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.350
Manager Inui.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.860
Touto Boys

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.860
Manager  Inui

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:01.950
What's going on?

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.180
Then, who will start for us tomorrow?

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:10.430
It's not like you to let 
a lead slip in this manner.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.580
I'm sorry.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.540
Oh well. It's a good learning experience.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.260
And tomorrow will be 
irrelevant if we lose today.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:21.940
Michiru.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.050
I've okayed it with the manager.

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:25.550
You're pitching.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.430
<i>Lineup change for the Touto Boys.</i>

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:38.750
<i>The pitcher, Komatsu-kun, will be replaced 
by first basewoman, Mayumura Michiru-san.</i>

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.360
<i>Komatsu-kun will replace her on first base.</i>

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.810
<i>Their ace has arrived...</i>

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:55.310
<i>Batting fifth, center field, Satou-kun.</i>

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.710
Center field

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.710
Satou Hikaru

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:00.570
Play!

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:08.720
Strike!

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:09.870
That's crazy fast!

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:11.860
So she's their ace!

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:15.790
A left-handed sidearm. 
That'll be hard to hit.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.320
Foul!

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.460
<i>The line that ball took was nuts...</i>

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.030
<i>I was sure it'd be a strike, 
but it veered off to the inside!</i>

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.900
<i>Huh. He managed to get something on it.</i>

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.040
Foul!

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.290
So close!

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:40.790
<i>This guy...</i>

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:45.400
<i>He's already tucking his arms in so that 
his swing meets the flight of the ball.</i>

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:47.710
<i>So annoying!</i>

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.050
Foul!

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:55.560
<i>He's something else! He's even
keeping up with Michiru's pitches!</i>

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.210
You're doing great, Hikaru!

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.850
You can hit these, Hikaru-kun!

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.290
<i>An unexpected switch to pitching.</i>

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:04.620
<i>Looks like she's still 
adjusting to being up there.</i>

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.110
<i>She's not quite in the zone yet.</i>

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.400
<i>If you include her practice pitches, 
she's thrown more than ten balls now.</i>

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:14.480
<i>Her arm should have warmed up by now.</i>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.090
Strike! Out!

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:30.750
Strike!

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.890
Strike! Out!

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:41.390
Mifune

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:41.390
Touto

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.240
Still tied.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:41.390
That was a real chance...

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:45.540
<i>We caught up, but this is 
where it gets really tough.</i>

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:48.130
<i>Getting runs off her won't be easy.</i>

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:50.400
<i>We can't afford to give up any runs, either.</i>

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:54.210
Manager, I apologize for 
getting us into this situation.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:59.160
Please send us signs for 
the final three innings.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.350
All right.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.130
<i>The Mifune Dolphins.</i>

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.170
<i>They were completely off my radar, 
but they've backed us into a corner.</i>

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:13.680
<i>Shigeno and Satou only joined the 
team right before this tournament.</i>

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:17.300
<i>The children of the two hopefuls
who clawed their way up</i>

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:22.160
<i>from Kaidou Academy's third team 
to the heady heights of the Majors.</i>

00:08:22.990 --> 00:08:26.540
<i>Let's see if they can 
live up to their namesakes.</i>

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:33.960
<i>Bottom of the fifth, Touto Boys to bat. 
Batting third, center field, Yue-kun.</i>

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:34.640
Yue, hang on a minute.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:41.320
Their battery will probably adjust their 
strategy based on our previous games.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.580
They probably know how good 
you are at hitting inside balls.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:49.970
So don't swing at any inside balls that 
look wayward. They're just padding.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:51.430
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:57.960
Ball two!

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.890
<i>We can't bait this guy.</i>

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.890
<i>They will bait you on the inside, and try 
to get you with lower outside balls.</i>

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.350
<i>Go for those.</i>

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.120
All right!

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.530
We got a runner on base!

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:18.030
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Mayumura-kun.</i>

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.820
<i>Damn it! We let a runner get 
on base in front of Mayumura.</i>

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:25.240
<i>With no outs and a runner on first, 
we can't walk him, either.</i>

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:29.290
<i>I won't let you get a hit! 
I </i>will<i> hold the line here!</i>

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:33.960
<i>This is the most pathetic game 
I've had since I put on the mask.</i>

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:36.660
<i>How dare you embarrass me...</i>

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.800
<i>I'm going to pay you back with my bat!</i>

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.640
Strike!

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:46.740
<i>Damn. That would have been a ball.</i>

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:52.310
<i>Huh?! A sacrifice bunt?!</i>

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.780
T-Time out, please!

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:58.320
Manager.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:01.470
I'm sorry, but did you just
give me the wrong sign?

00:10:01.470 --> 00:10:03.950
I gave you the sign for a sacrifice bunt.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.110
Is something wrong?

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:09.560
You're wondering why a cleanup 
would have to play a sacrifice bunt.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:14.210
I sent that sign because, after seeing your 
swing just now, I know you won't get a hit.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:16.420
Manager!

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:17.470
Wataru.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:22.430
Calling the shots alone does not 
mean you're playing baseball alone.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:26.680
You thought you could beat a team 
where everyone's pulling together?

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:30.850
Forget about the instruction to bunt.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:32.000
Just go out there.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.070
You know what to do, don't you?

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.050
Yes, sir!

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:38.760
Play!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.290
Ball!

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:46.800
<i>What's this?</i>

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.360
<i>I don't like the way he turned that down.</i>

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:52.080
<i>Watch out, Urabe.</i>

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.090
<i>Don't go easy on this guy!</i>

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:57.240
<i>I don't need a big hit.</i>

00:10:59.130 --> 00:10:59.880
<i>Just to follow up!</i>

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:03.700
It got through!

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.350
No outs, runners on first and second!

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:06.810
Crap.

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:10.690
<i>Batting fifth, right field, Kouzaka-kun.</i>

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.070
First!

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:22.280
I won't let you!

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:24.370
Safe!

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.370
S-Sorry.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.330
All right!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.250
No outs and bases loaded!

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:43.020
<i>Crap. We'd just caught up, too...</i>

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:46.710
<i>Batting sixth, left field, Kotouge-kun.</i>

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:51.810
Go!

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:55.730
Safe!

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:58.190
All right! Let's bring this win home!

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:03.950
D-Don't worry about it!

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.700
<i>Batting seventh, third base, Nakamura-kun.</i>

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.150
It's only one run!

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:10.510
Don't let it get to you!

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:12.160
Stay sharp, battery!

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:16.780
<i>You say that, Manager, 
but that run was a killer.</i>

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.700
<i>Taking two runs off Mayumura Michiru is...</i>

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:30.850
Out!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:35.180
My bad. I totally wasn't ready for that.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:37.790
Nice running!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.480
A squeeze play right back at 'em!

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:41.900
<i>That's two runs we've bagged as a team.</i>

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.420
<i>This is huge!</i>

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.630
<i>The game's definitely 
turned in our favor now!</i>

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:50.480
<i>With our brilliant manager
and the players we've got,</i>

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.460
<i>there's no way we can lose this!</i>

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:57.750
Out!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:00.550
Mifune

00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:00.550
Touto

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:00.080
Three outs! Change sides!

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.360
I'm so sorry, guys.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:14.420
You all gave it everything to get us 
within touching distance, and yet...

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:15.810
I'm so very sorry.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:18.860
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.290
It's not over yet!

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.030
We can still get those two runs back!

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:24.340
We can't give up now, guys!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:26.440
Y-Yeah, you're right!

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:28.350
Right! It's time to attack!

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:31.510
Strike! Out!

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:37.050
Three outs...

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:38.950
She's struck out five people in a row.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:43.220
<i>How are we going to get any runs off her?</i>

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.090
Ball.

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.200
Ball four.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.100
They got another run.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:11.830
Right field!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.160
Out!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.920
Three outs. Change sides!

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.630
Mifune

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:21.630
Touto

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:23.250
All right. It's the final inning.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.390
Let's wrap this up!

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:25.590
Yeah!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:28.020
That insurance run put 
them even further ahead.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.590
They're now three runs behind.

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:32.800
Yeah, it was never going to be easy.

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:34.980
This team can't be beaten with just luck.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.140
You guys have been great out there.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:44.150
I'll be honest: I didn't think we'd hold 
out against Touto as well as we have.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.250
It won't be easy to score 
three runs off that pitcher,

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:49.510
but since this is the final inning,

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:51.660
just go out and swing with no regrets!

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:52.990
Yes, sir!

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.160
Shortstop

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.160
Kimura

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:57.160
<i>Batting first, shortstop. Kimura-kun.</i>

00:14:57.800 --> 00:14:59.130
<i>Three left.</i>

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:05.790
Strike!

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:08.340
Nagai.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.480
If we get to two outs, you're pinch-hitting.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.390
Get ready.

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:15.060
Nagai

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:14.650
Y-Yessir!

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:21.660
<i>It's not over yet.</i>

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:25.360
<i>If we can hang on until Hikaru's turn, 
three runs isn't impossible.</i>

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:30.780
Strike! Out!

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.490
<i>Batting second, left field, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:44.020
<i>After I bunted three times, 
they're not taking any chances.</i>

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.230
<i>I really need a hit this time.</i>

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:49.270
<i>I need to get on base, no matter what!</i>

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:54.760
<i>If Shigeno falls now, they'll put Nagai in 
to bat instead of me and the game's over.</i>

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.430
<i>Looks like the mountain known as 
Touto was steeper than I thought.</i>

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.080
Strike!

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:11.210
Mayumura Michiru has struck
six people out since they put her in.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:13.470
If Satou's the only one who 
can even graze her pitches,

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.890
there's not much we can do.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:18.960
<i>In the end, we lost because 
they managed to hit my pitches.</i>

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:22.370
<i>I just want to get outta here now.</i>

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:26.460
Ball!

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:28.490
<i>He's got a good eye.</i>

00:16:28.490 --> 00:16:31.460
<i>Or maybe he just couldn't swing in time?</i>

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:34.880
<i>Let's give him one more ball 
to make sure which it is.</i>

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:40.970
Ball!

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:42.760
<i>Damn...</i>

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.400
<i>He's actually reading them.</i>

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:47.440
Good job, Daigo-kun!

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:48.940
Nice, nice!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:52.550
Wow, he's got the measure of those pitches!

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:54.690
He was practicing bunts until 
sundown with Urabe-kun,

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:58.570
simulating all those 
left-handed sidearm throws.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:03.660
I guess he's just not as scared 
of her pitches than the others.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:07.430
Well, whatever. Just 'cause he can judge 
them, doesn't mean he can hit them.

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:09.910
<i>I need to get on base!</i>

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:12.670
<i>I don't want this to be over yet!</i>

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:16.760
Foul, foul!

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:18.210
<i>I actually touched it!</i>

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:25.070
Foul.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:26.550
You're hitting them!

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.130
Hit it, Shigeno-kun!

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:30.400
<i>Hey, now...</i>

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:36.050
<i>Stop it. Just stop, already!</i>

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:38.030
<i>Why are you still fighting so hard?!</i>

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.600
<i>We already know they've won!</i>

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.120
<i>Just let the game end already!</i>

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:46.800
Foul, foul!

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:48.580
<i>Damn!</i>

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:54.310
<i>He couldn't even get near them before.</i>

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.100
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:01.100
Ball!

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:03.350
Three balls, two strikes!

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.810
All right! It's a full count!

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:09.390
<i>Straight down the middle.</i>

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:10.600
<i>Don't let him walk.</i>

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:14.620
<i>He's struggling to even touch them. 
There's no way he'll get a proper hit!</i>

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.360
Ball!

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.530
Ball four!

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:23.350
All right!

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:24.540
Nice eye!

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.970
<i>Batting third, pitcher. Urabe-kun.</i>

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:31.170
Guess I'm staying on the bench for now.

00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:33.460
Go get 'em, Urabe-kun!

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:37.670
Come on, Urabe!

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:39.740
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:42.620
<i>I can't believe that idiot 
actually got on base.</i>

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:45.100
<i>He's just a beginner.</i>

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.940
<i>He refuses to give up and 
doesn't know when to quit.</i>

00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:57.450
Foul!

00:18:57.450 --> 00:19:01.380
<i>No, </i>because<i> he's a beginner, 
he doesn't know his own limits yet.</i>

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.550
<i>But you get it now, right?</i>

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:07.580
Strike!

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.870
Mifune

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.870
Touto

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:11.830
<i>We can catch up to them, time and again, 
but they'll just keep on pulling ahead!</i>

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:16.590
<i>When you find out that their lineup, their 
training, and everything else is a cut above,</i>

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:19.170
<i>it should crush you straight away!</i>

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:20.090
<i>It really should!</i>

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.060
<i>And yet, still...</i>

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:29.890
I can't keep playing for the Touto Boys.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:36.210
As long as <i>he's</i> there, 
I'll never be the ace

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:39.440
I want to join another team and defeat him.

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:41.450
Oh, so that's why.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.950
Then, I'll come with you to the Dolphins.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.750
<i>You really don't know when to give up!</i>

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.160
<i>You third-rate "second!"</i>

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.820
Safe! Safe!

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.260
Yeah!

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:20.940
Urabe followed it up!

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:23.070
One out, runners on first and second!

00:20:24.600 --> 00:20:27.780
I guess I don't know when to give up, either.

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:30.290
They're hanging on.

00:20:30.690 --> 00:20:32.660
They're hoping to get one more chance.

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.500
Whatever. Your pitching's good.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:42.010
It was sheer luck that he hit it at 
an angle that kept it in fair territory.

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:44.940
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:20:44.940 --> 00:20:46.820
Watch out on your first throw.

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:49.440
If we get these next 
two out, victory is ours.

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:51.270
Okay!

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:54.740
Play!

00:20:58.100 --> 00:20:59.480
Strike!

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:03.990
<i>They're even more impressive up close.</i>

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:10.230
Oh, right. Those pitches are one thing for 
a right-hander, but for a lefty like Andy...

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:14.430
Yeah. The balls coming at him 
must feel quite natural.

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:17.750
Strike two!

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:21.510
<i>Good! We've got them now!</i>

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.100
<i>That second run we conceded in the fifth</i>

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:26.660
<i>was my fault because I wasn't 
watching for the squeeze play.</i>

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:31.300
<i>I made the mistake. Now, I have 
to make up for it with my bat!</i>

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:33.000
Foul!

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:34.440
Good job!

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.560
Second base

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.560
Katsumata

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.560
First base

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.560
Matsubara

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:35.560
Go!

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:37.810
Hit it, Andy!

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.890
<i>I joined the Dolphins to 
defeat the Touto Boys.</i>

00:21:41.460 --> 00:21:44.530
<i>Our entire team has pulled 
together to create this chance.</i>

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:47.410
<i>If I couldn't live up to 
everyone's expectations here...</i>

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:49.570
<i>...I wouldn't be playing cleanup!</i>

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:55.120
Wh-What?!

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:56.250
Yes!

00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:58.490
Awesome!

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.840
Stop, stop!

00:22:06.690 --> 00:22:08.420
Bases... loaded?

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:13.810
<i>Batting fifth, center field. Satou-kun.</i>

00:22:18.910 --> 00:22:22.680
<i>Last time, he hit a liner off 
Komatsu's fastball and got us good.</i>

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:28.150
<i>But I won't let you get 
any more hits, Satou Hikaru!</i>

00:24:00.690 --> 00:24:03.480
The final inning. One out, and bases loaded.

00:24:03.480 --> 00:24:06.010
Everybody's hearts came 
together to create this chance.

00:24:06.420 --> 00:24:07.800
We have to catch up here or it's over!

00:24:08.470 --> 00:24:10.470
Hikaru, please, hit it!

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:15.050
But the pitch their ace, 
Mayumura Michiru, throws is...

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:18.060
The game against the Touto 
Boys is about to be decided!

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
The Hit of Destiny

00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:21.510
Next time: "The Hit of Destiny."

00:24:21.510 --> 00:24:23.620
Run to the stage of your dreams!
